Feature: Original Native Prepared Population
  Scenario: One immutable source and private index serve multiple clause cursors
    Given an original admitted request donor and snapshot source
    When the original caller prepares the population under all original currencies
    Then the donor moves once and two turn callbacks borrow the same actual source and index
    And exact IDs preserve original ordinals and ambiguity
    And container preparation does not certify schema or publication

  Scenario: Rejected identity substitution has no effects
    Given a pending or prepared original population
    When another request, source, caller or epoch is offered
    Then the original owner and donor remain stationary
    And no retained receipt or heap allocation occurs

  Scenario: Every cancelled prefix closes through original custody
    Given every funded preparation or completed callback prefix
    When cancellation or an ordinary deadline prevents further work
    Then no view or partial output is published
    And paid original close retires index metadata before snapshot and request owners

  Scenario: Unavailable containers retain request-only diagnostics
    Given the actual admitted request and an unavailable original container
    When a clause copies its caller-authored target labels under the original context
    Then a one-turn request-only borrow exposes the exact original request
    And no graph or prepared-index accessor is supplied
    And pending or unavailable input cannot manufacture a prepared view

  Scenario: Wrapper admission donates its original born source lease
    Given the wrapper retains one original-paid snapshot Arc before reading the model
    When request admission completes and the snapshot donor is received
    Then the exact donor moves before the receipt is posted
    And no second snapshot alias is created
    And refusal leaves both donors and the population stationary

